<Layout title="Resources" description="A small toolkit grounded in this project's actual implementation, plus a checklist for choosing fewer, more useful tools." active="Resources"><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Use what you need</p><h1>A small toolkit.<br />Not a shopping list.</h1><p class="lead">These are tools used to build this project. Start with a job to do, then choose a tool. You may already have enough.</p><p class="small">No affiliate links, paid placements or sponsored recommendations on this page.</p></header><section class="section" aria-label="Project toolkit"><div class="resource"><h2>Astro</h2><div><p>This site's pages are built with Astro. A static publishing approach suits a handful of guides without accounts or a database.</p><p>Use your existing publishing system if it already makes editing easy. A framework migration needs a better reason than novelty.</p></div></div><div class="resource"><h2>Git &amp; GitHub</h2><div><p>The project keeps code and text changes in version control. Reviewing a diff makes it easier to understand what changed and recover earlier work.</p><p>Keep secrets and private business records out of a public repository. Version control is not a substitute for an independent backup of private files.</p></div></div><div class="resource"><h2>Cloudflare Pages</h2><div><p>The existing stockswatch.cc site uses Cloudflare Pages. Keeping the same hosting avoids introducing another service just to publish these guides.</p><p>Check your own usage and billing before assuming hosting is free. This list makes no promise about a provider's current pricing.</p></div></div><div class="resource"><h2>Playwright</h2><div><p>This project uses browser checks for navigation, mobile layouts and accessibility. The useful question is whether a reader can complete the intended task.</p><p>A passing automated test is only part of the picture. Read the page, use the keyboard and inspect it at a narrow screen size too.</p></div></div></section><aside class="callout"><h2>Before adding another tool</h2><p>What task will it improve? What does it cost in money and attention? Can an existing tool do the job? How will you export your work or stop using it?</p><a href="/guides/before-you-automate.html">Start with the automation checklist ↗</a></aside></div></Layout>
